<SiteLayout title="Methodology | Nordic Systems" description="How Nordic Systems distinguishes sources, inference, and speculation in architecture maps.">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"><h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold">Methodology</h1><p class="mt-5 text-slate-700">Nordic Systems creates original reconstructions of architecture from public material. We do not claim that any company’s architecture is verified by the company unless a source explicitly supports a specific claim.</p><h2 class="mt-9 text-2xl font-semibold">Claim statuses</h2><dl class="mt-4 space-y-4"><div><dt class="font-semibold">Documented</dt><dd class="text-slate-700">A claim linked to at least one public source.</dd></div><div><dt class="font-semibold">Inferred</dt><dd class="text-slate-700">A reasoned interpretation. Its rationale is included so readers can assess it.</dd></div><div><dt class="font-semibold">Speculative</dt><dd class="text-slate-700">A possibility that lacks enough evidence to present as an inference or fact.</dd></div></dl><h2 class="mt-9 text-2xl font-semibold">Confidence and time</h2><p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">Confidence describes how strongly the available evidence supports a claim; it is not a guarantee. As-of dates state the latest time the claim is intended to represent. Claims older than three years receive a “May be outdated” warning, including when only a year or month is known.</p><h2 class="mt-9 text-2xl font-semibold">Sources and original work</h2><p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">We choose public engineering posts, talks, documentation, and open-source material that directly help support a claim. When an archived URL is available, we link it alongside the original. Summaries and diagrams are written and drawn by Nordic Systems; we do not copy source text or diagrams.</p><h2 class="mt-9 text-2xl font-semibold">Suggest a correction</h2><p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">If a source is missing, stale, or misread, please <a class="underline" href="https://github.com/your-org/nordic-systems/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">open a GitHub issue (placeholder)</a> with the relevant public evidence.</p></article>
</SiteLayout>
